<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Client> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4syst/System> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Software entity which represents a Device by exposing its DM Functions to one or more DM Server(s). \n\nIt is responsible for the triggering of the DM Functions when a Command targetting the represented Device is received by the Server. The Client is also responsible for the reporting of the results of the Function execution to the Server.\n\nThe Client has an identifier that is unique only relatively to each Server it is connected to."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Client"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DatamodelParameterCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DatamodelParameterCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DatamodelParameterCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DatamodelParameterCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of one or more Datamodel Parameters."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DatamodelParameterCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Datamodel Parameter Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceControlCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceControlCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceControlCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceControlCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of the device state, for instance the power state with a Reboot or Shutdown command."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceControlCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Control Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceIdentityCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceIdentityCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceIdentityCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceIdentityCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of device identification properties."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceIdentityCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Identity Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Command> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of Commands that are specific to the Device Management domain."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Management Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementFunctionCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementFunctionCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementFunctionCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Function> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementFunctionCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of Functions related to the Device Management domain.\n\nThese Functions correspond to the capabilities of the Device to perform its own diagnostics, maintenance, configuration, monitoring and control."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementFunctionCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Management Function Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/State> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This is a class of states for Device Management."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Management State"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModule
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/FeatureOfInterest> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A DeviceModule is an executable software entity on the Device, i.e., a DeviceModule may be activated and deactivated on demand through dedicated Functions.\n\nAs such, the DeviceModule implements specific Functions that are available to the Device when the DeviceModule is activated.\n\nA DeviceModule is supported by a DevicePackage: deleting the corresponding DevicePackage will in turn remove the DeviceModule and its related Functions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Module"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModuleState
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModuleState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModuleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModuleState> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackageState> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModuleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "State of a DeviceModule"@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceModuleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Module State"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackage
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/FeatureOfInterest> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A DevicePackage is an archive file that may contain resource files, code, libraries or executable files.\nIt is a resource that the Device should retrieve or receive from an external source.\n\nA DevicePackage is only actionable once it has been downloaded and installed.\n\nIt may allow a Device to support additional Functions by instantiating a DeviceModule.\n\nA DevicePackage may be uninstalled and then removed from the Device."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Package"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackageState
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackageState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackageState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementState> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackageState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "State of a DevicePackage"@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DevicePackageState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Device Package State"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#FirmwareManagementCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#FirmwareManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#FirmwareManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#FirmwareManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of device firmwares."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#FirmwareManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Firmware Management Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManageableDevice
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManageableDevice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManageableDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Device> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManageableDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A tangible object that has at least one Device Management Function.\n\nThis class extends the saref:Device class, it is a Feature of Interest by definition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManageableDevice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manageable Device"@en .
