<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementConnection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Abstract representation of the connection between a Client and a Server. It does not necessarily imply that a persistent connection is established between the entities - such as a TCP connection. It represents the link and the capability of the Server to interact with the Client.\n\nFor instance, the Client has been authenticated by the Server with a certificate, and/or the client has received a configuration for access rights to its functions for the Server."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementConnection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Management Connection"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementService
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementService> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Service> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A saref:Service that represents functions or functions of interest of the Device Management Function Category.\n\nThe ManagementService exposes these functions through a Connection, between a Client and a Server."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ManagementService> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Management Service"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ModuleManagementCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ModuleManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ModuleManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ModuleManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of device modules."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#ModuleManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Module Management Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#PackageManagementCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#PackageManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#PackageManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#PackageManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of device packages."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#PackageManagementCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Package Management Command Category"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Server
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Server> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Server> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://saref.etsi.org/saref4syst/System> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Server> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A DM Server is the software entity which is responsible for performing DM operations on a fleet of Devices. It exposes the set of available operations to an entity that needs to trigger an operation, such as a manufacturer or a Customer Care service. \n\nThe DM Server is a endpoint, generally secured, with which DM Clients communicate. \n\nThe protocol used between Server and Client is not in the scope of this ontology. It can follow a DM standard such as CWMP or LWM2M, or be completely proprietary."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#Server> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Server"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelCommandCategory
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#DeviceManagementCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Category of commands enabling the manipulation of supported datamodels."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelCommandCategory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supported Datamodel Command Category"@en .
