# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterProperty
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterProperty> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Property> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Property kind that represents the properties of a Supported Datamodel Parameter.\n\nThese parameters represent the capabilities of the Device in a format specific to the datamodel implemented by the Device, and exposed by the Client.\n\nIt should not be confused with the Datamodel Parameter Instance, which represents the actionable capabilities of the Device."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterProperty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supported datamodel parameter property"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterType
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://saref.etsi.org/core/Property> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Type of a supported datamodel parameter. \n\nFor instance, this type can represent that the supported datamodel parameter is a reference to an executable resource. The corresponding type would be 'command' in the CWMP standard protocol, and its TR-181 technical report.\n\nThis type can represent a reference to a measurement process on the device that retrieves a value. In that case, the supported datamodel parameter also describes the unit of that value.\n\nThe type 'object' corresponds to a supported datamodel parameter that contains other supported datamodel parameters, creating a hierarchical structure.\n\nA final example would be a 'table', i.e., the corresponding datamodel parameter is a list of instances of the same object.\n\nFor more information, we refer the reader to the specification documents of DM protocol standards such as TR-181 from the BroadBand Forum."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelParameterType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supported datamodel parameter type"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelRetrievalCommand
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelRetrievalCommand> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelRetrievalCommand> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelCommandCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelRetrievalCommand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Command to retrieve a supported datamodel parameter, which corresponds to the information required to access a datamodel parameter instance and interpret its value."@en .
<https://w3id.org/dmont/ontology#SupportedDatamodelRetrievalCommand> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Supported datamodel retrieval command"@en .
